Keep the Code Action list open when the soft keyboard goes down.

CodeActionController hides the list on every layout change of its editor,
because the list sits at page coordinates taken when it opened. On Android
the soft keyboard goes down whenever focus leaves text, and the list takes
focus from the editor as it opens, so with the keyboard up a tap on the light
bulb made the window grow under the list, the editor's layout changed, and
the list closed, its onHide giving the editor focus back. On an API 37
emulator with Gboard 17.7.4 the list was on screen for 277 ms. The page's
keyboard guard asked for nothing there, and the same close happened in
headless Chromium with an Android user agent and no guard at all, when the
viewport grew by the height of a keyboard.

On Android a change of the editor's height alone now leaves the list open.
The editor grows downward when the keyboard goes down, so the light bulb and
the list beside it stay where they were. A change of width, as a turn of the
phone makes, still closes it, and elsewhere every layout change does, as
before.

Verified in headless Chromium with an Android user agent: opened from the
light bulb, the list stayed open beside it while the viewport grew from 460
to 845 pixels, where the bundle without this patch closed it and focused the
editor; a tap on a row then applied that row and gave the editor focus back;
a viewport turned to landscape closed the list in both bundles; and with a
desktop user agent the list closed at the height change, as before. The same
edit was first tried over the minified bundle, then built. With the built
tree on API 33 and 37 emulators, with Gboard 12.4 and 17.7.4, the list opened
from the light bulb with the keyboard up stayed open while the keyboard went
down, and a tap outside it closed it.

